{{was wotd|2023|March|6}}

===Etymology===
[[File:Rob Gronkowski.JPG|thumb|The [[American#Adjective|American]] retired [[American football|football]] tight end ''({{senseno|en|player}})'' {{w|Rob Gronkowski}} who played in the {{w|National Football League}} for 11 seasons with the {{w|New England Patriots}} and the {{w|Tampa Bay Buccaneers}}.]]

From {{compound|en|tight|t1=of a space, arrangement, etc.: narrow, such that it is difficult for something or someone to pass through it|end|t2=position at the end of either the offensive or defensive line; player playing this position|notext=1|type=endocentric}}, from the fact that the player takes up a position close to the [[tackle#Noun|tackle]].<ref>{{R:OED Online|subpos=n|subid=18413632|entry=tight|pos=''adj.'', ''adv.'', and ''n.''{{sup|2}}|noformat=1|id=201925|date=December 2022}}</ref><ref>{{R:Dictionary.com|pos=n|source=Random House}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ˌtaɪt ˈɛnd/}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛnd|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|American football}} {{defdate|from 1960s}}
## {{senseid|en|American position}} The [[position#Noun|position]] at the [[end#Noun|end]] of the [[offensive line]] whose [[primary]] [[job#Noun|jobs]] are to [[block#Verb|block]] and [[serve#Verb|serve]] as a [[short#Adjective|short]] [[receiver]].
##: {{ux|en|Jones played '''tight end'''.}}
## {{senseid|en|player}} A [[player]] (called an end) playing the position of tight end ''({{senseno|en|American position}})''.
##: {{ux|en|The '''tight end''' caught the pass.}}
# {{lb|en|Canadian football|historical}}
## {{senseid|en|Canadian position}} The position at the end of the offensive line whose primary jobs were to block and serve as a short receiver; this position is no longer [[use#Verb|used]].
## A player (called an end) playing the position of tight end ''({{senseno|en|Canadian position}})''.

